From 7154d82cc45f4e69399f0446404ab79ad5100ed2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julian Cooper <115541810+Juliansgith@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:09:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/52] Draw projectile launch spreads like the binary does

Replaying an FAF (3839) recording showed the rebuild's random stream
falling behind the shipped engine's on the first beat that created a
projectile. Entity:CreateProjectile with no direction and
CreateProjectileAtBone draw the blueprint spreads through
FUN_0051C400 (position), FUN_0051C510 (direction) and an inlined
launch-speed spread; each lane is CRandomStream::FRand(-range, range)
plus the base lane, and each draws a twister word even when its range
is zero. The recovery:

- skipped the draw for zero ranges (the commander warp-in effect's
  direction spread: three words per projectile), which shifted every
  later random number;
- scaled a float-rounded word instead of multiplying the exact word
  (MulTwisterWord), and used an approximate 2^-32 in double for the
  position spread;
- normalized the launch direction and the bone-forward fallback, which
  the binary does not do (COORDS_Orient normalizes its own copy), and
  compared the direction to zero with operator== instead of the
  binary's 12-byte memcmp.

RProjectileBlueprint now has GetRandomLaunchOffset (0x0051C400) and
GetRandomLaunchDirection (0x0051C510), and its other spread samplers
(lifetime, speeds, turn rate, mesh scale) use the exact FRand.

Lua's Random() with no arguments (0x00759143) is the word times the
float 2^-32 under _PC_24; the recovery multiplied by the double
2.3283064e-10, which is not 2^-32, and came out one float low for about
one call in a hundred.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
